.docname {Dashboard Service}
.include {docs}

.glossary
    | Word | Meaning | Example |
    |---|---|---|
    | Column | One field the dashboard table shows for a building | `temperature`, `roomName` |
    | Preferences | The list of columns one building shows | `["roomName","roomMaxOccupancy","temperature"]` |
    | Catalog | Every metric any service can report, used to fill the column picker | temperature, airQuality, peopleCount |
    | Tick | Everything one building reports at one moment, one message | See Telemetry Schema |
    | Tunnel | The background loop that reads every tick and forwards it to its building's channel | `tunnel.rs` |
    | `DashMap` | A map many tasks can read and write at once without one big lock | building id → columns |
    | Fire and forget | Start a task and do not wait for its result | The MongoDB write after a save |

Rust, Axum, Tokio, MongoDB, Redis. Directory `backend/dashboard`. Role and choices: [Dashboard architecture](../architecture/dashboard-architecture.qd).

Two jobs in one process:

| Job | Entry | Reads | Writes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Column preferences and catalog | HTTP, `api/` | `DashMap`, `/contracts` of other services | `DashMap`, MongoDB |
| Route each tick to its building | `tunnel.rs`, Redis | `telemetry:raw`, `DashMap` | `telemetry:filtered:{buildingId}` |

---

## Layout

Flat on purpose: no domain rules worth layers, so no hexagon and no layering test.

| Path | Holds |
|---|---|
| `src/main.rs` | Start-up: connect MongoDB, fill the `DashMap`, start the tunnel, serve HTTP |
| `src/state.rs` | `AppState`: `building_preferences: Arc<DashMap<String, Vec<String>>>` and the MongoDB collection |
| `src/models.rs` | `PreferenceDocument`; re-exports `MetricContract`, `MetricsDiscoveryResponse` from `telemetry-schema` |
| `src/api/dashboard.rs` | `GET /`: the catalog |
| `src/api/data.rs` | `GET` and `POST /preferences/{building_id}` |
| `src/api/init.rs` | `POST /preferences/init/{building_id}`: starting columns |
| `src/tunnel.rs` | `start_telemetry_tunnel`, `listen_and_fanout`, `resolve_channel`, `process_and_publish` |
| `src/infra/db.rs` | `connect`, `load_all`, `upsert_preference` |
| `src/infra/discovery.rs` | `discover_services`: reads `*_METRICS_URL` |
| `src/infra/claims.rs` | `GatewayClaims` extractor |
| `src/infra/metrics.rs` | Prometheus counters, `/metrics`, `/health` |

---

## Start-up

.mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant M as main.rs
        participant DB as infra/db.rs
        participant Mo as MongoDB
        participant S as AppState
        participant T as tunnel.rs
        participant R as Redis
        M->>DB: connect(MONGO_URI)
        DB->>Mo: database crowdvision, collection preferences
        DB->>Mo: create unique index on building_id
        M->>S: AppState::new(collection), empty DashMap
        M->>DB: load_all(collection)
        DB->>Mo: find all documents
        Mo-->>M: one document per building
        M->>S: insert building_id and allowed_columns for each
        M->>T: start_telemetry_tunnel(REDIS_URL, state)
        T->>R: open a pub/sub connection and a publish connection
        T->>T: tokio::spawn(listen_and_fanout)
        M->>M: bind 0.0.0.0:PORT, axum::serve with graceful shutdown

| Step | Fails | Result |
|---|---|---|
| 1 to 3 | MongoDB down, index refused | Panic: `Failed to connect to MongoDB`. The pod restarts |
| 5 to 7 | Read fails | Panic: `Failed to load preferences from MongoDB` |
| 9 to 10 | Redis down | Logged, tunnel returns. HTTP still starts, but **no tick is forwarded** until restart |
| 12 | Port taken | Logged: `Failed to bind to port` |

- The `DashMap` is full before the first request. A restart shows what MongoDB holds, nothing more.
- The tunnel never reconnects. A Redis restart after start-up stops the live feed until `dashboard` restarts.

---

## Routes

The edge strips `/dashboard` (`handle_path` in the `Caddyfile`), so `/dashboard/preferences/b1` arrives as `/preferences/b1`.

| Method | Path | Who calls | Does |
|---|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/` | `client`, `useColumnManager.ts` | Catalog of every metric. `{"metrics": [MetricContract, …]}` |
| `GET` | `/preferences/{building_id}` | `client` | `{building_id, allowed_columns}`, or `404` when unknown |
| `POST` | `/preferences/{building_id}` | `client` | Replace the columns. Body `{allowed_columns}` |
| `POST` | `/preferences/init/{building_id}` | `digital-twin`, after a registration | Give a new building its starting columns |
| `GET` | `/metrics` | Prometheus | Counters and latency |
| `GET` | `/health` | Probes | `200`, empty body |

Every route except `/metrics` and `/health` takes `GatewayClaims`:

1. Read header `x-gateway-claims` (`claims_schema::CLAIMS_HEADER`). Missing: `401`.
2. Decode base64 (standard or URL-safe) JSON into `ClaimsPayload`. Fails: `401`.
3. No `sub`: `401`.
4. The claims are not used further. **Any signed-in person may read or change any building's columns.**

---

## Reading and saving columns

.mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant C as client
        participant E as edge
        participant A as api/data.rs
        participant S as DashMap
        participant Mo as MongoDB
        C->>E: POST /dashboard/preferences/b1 {"allowed_columns":[…3 names…]}
        E->>A: POST /preferences/b1, x-gateway-claims
        A->>A: GatewayClaims, then update_preferences
        A->>S: insert b1 with the 3 columns
        A->>A: tokio::spawn(upsert_preference)
        A-->>C: 200 {"status":"success","building_id":"b1","active_columns":3}
        A->>Mo: find_one_and_replace building_id b1, upsert
        Note over A,Mo: a failure here is only logged
        C->>A: GET /preferences/b1
        A->>S: get b1
        A-->>C: 200 {"building_id":"b1","allowed_columns":[…]}

| Step | Data |
|---|---|
| 1 | `{"allowed_columns":["roomName","roomMaxOccupancy","temperature"]}` |
| 4 | `DashMap["b1"] = ["roomName","roomMaxOccupancy","temperature"]` |
| 6 | `active_columns` is the **count**, `3`, not the list |
| 7 | MongoDB `{_id, building_id:"b1", allowed_columns:[…]}`, one document per building |

- **`200` does not mean saved.** Step 6 answers before step 7 runs. If step 7 fails, or the pod stops between 6 and 7, the change lives only in memory and is lost at the next restart.
- The body is not checked: an empty list, an unknown name or a duplicate is stored as sent.
- `GET` reads only the `DashMap`, never MongoDB.

---

## Starting columns

.mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant Tw as digital-twin<br/>outbound.rs
        participant I as api/init.rs
        participant S as DashMap
        participant Mo as MongoDB
        Tw->>I: POST /preferences/init/b1, creator's claims
        I->>S: entry(b1), or_insert_with(DEFAULT_COLUMNS)
        alt b1 was not there
            I->>I: tokio::spawn(upsert_preference)
            I->>Mo: upsert ["roomName","roomMaxOccupancy"]
        else b1 already had columns
            I->>I: keep them, write nothing
        end
        I-->>Tw: 200

- `DEFAULT_COLUMNS` = `roomName`, `roomMaxOccupancy`.
- Calling twice is safe: `or_insert_with` runs the default only when the key is missing, in one atomic step.
- `digital-twin` calls it only when its `sync_enabled` is on. A failed call is logged there as `failed to init building preferences`, and nothing retries it.

.box {A building with no columns gets no live feed} type:{warning}
    The tunnel drops every tick for a building missing from the `DashMap`. If the init call above fails, the building shows no live data until someone saves its columns once.

---

## The catalog

.mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant C as client
        participant A as api/dashboard.rs
        participant D as infra/discovery.rs
        participant T as telemetry
        participant Tw as digital-twin
        C->>A: GET /dashboard
        A->>D: discover_services()
        D-->>A: values of every *_METRICS_URL env var
        A->>A: collect_metrics: one reqwest client, 2 s timeout
        par join_all
            A->>T: fetch_service_metrics: GET http://telemetry:3000/contracts
            T-->>A: {"service":"telemetry","metrics":[…]}
        and
            A->>Tw: fetch_service_metrics: GET http://digital-twin:3000/contracts
            Tw-->>A: {"service":"digital-twin","metrics":[…]}
        end
        A->>A: fill missing source, then push_unique_metric one by one
        A-->>C: 200 {"metrics":[…]}

.mermaid
    flowchart TD
        U["one source URL"] --> G{"GET /contracts answers in 2 s?"}
        G -- no --> L1["log Failed to reach, empty list"]
        G -- yes --> P{"body parses as MetricsDiscoveryResponse?"}
        P -- no --> L2["log Failed to deserialize, empty list"]
        P -- "object {service, metrics}" --> S1["source = service, when missing"]
        P -- "bare list" --> S2["source = the URL, when missing"]
        S1 --> D{"same kind, interface and source already in the list?"}
        S2 --> D
        D -- yes --> Skip["skip"]
        D -- no --> Add["add"]

- Sources: `SENSOR_METRICS_URL=http://telemetry:3000` and `TWIN_METRICS_URL=http://digital-twin:3000`, in both compose and Kubernetes. A new source is an env var, not a code change.
- The catalog is fetched on **every** request. Nothing is cached.
- A failed source never fails the request: the answer is `200` with fewer metrics. The only trace is the log line.

**Example.** `digital-twin` hangs. After 2 s its fetch gives up. The client gets `200` with the 3 `telemetry` metrics, and the log says `Failed to reach http://digital-twin:3000/contracts`.

Shapes and parsing rules: [Telemetry Schema, the metric catalog](../packages/telemetry-schema.qd).

---

## The tunnel

.mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant R as Redis
        participant L as listen_and_fanout
        participant P as process_and_publish
        participant S as DashMap
        R->>L: message on telemetry:raw
        L->>L: get_payload as String, skip if not text
        L->>L: serde_json::from_str into TelemetryEnvelope
        L->>P: task::spawn(envelope, original text)
        P->>P: EVENTS_RECEIVED + 1
        P->>S: resolve_channel: contains_key(buildingId)?
        P->>R: PUBLISH telemetry:filtered:{buildingId}, original text
        P->>P: FANOUT_LATENCY_MS observe now minus ingestedAt
        P->>P: EVENTS_PUBLISHED + 1

.mermaid
    flowchart TD
        M["message"] --> T{"text?"}
        T -- no --> X0["skip silently"]
        T -- yes --> E{"TelemetryEnvelope?"}
        E -- no --> X1["log not a tick envelope, skip"]
        E -- yes --> K{"buildingId in DashMap?"}
        K -- no --> X2["log No preferences found, drop<br/>received counted, published not"]
        K -- yes --> Pub["PUBLISH original text"]

| Rule | Why |
|---|---|
| One task per message | A slow publish never holds up the next message |
| Original text republished | `dashboard` needs only `buildingId` to route. It does not own the reading fields |
| No metric filter | Every metric of a known building goes through. The columns only decide what the table shows, in the browser |
| Own building only | A tick goes to the channel of its own `buildingId`, never another |
| Publish result ignored | A failed `PUBLISH` is not logged. `EVENTS_PUBLISHED` still counts it |

**Example.** 3 ticks arrive: building `b1` (has columns), building `b9` (no columns), and the text `hello`.

| Tick | `telemetry_events_received_total` | Published on | `telemetry_events_published_total` |
|---|---|---|---|
| `b1` | +1 | `telemetry:filtered:b1` | +1 |
| `b9` | +1 | nothing | +0 |
| `hello` | +0 | nothing | +0 |

The whole path, from `telemetry` to the browser: [Telemetry Schema, a tick end to end](../packages/telemetry-schema.qd).

---

## Configuration

| Variable | Default | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `MONGO_URI` | `mongodb://localhost:27017` | MongoDB server. The database name is fixed in code: `crowdvision`, collection `preferences` |
| `REDIS_URL` | `redis://127.0.0.1/` | Tunnel in and out |
| `PORT` | `3000` | HTTP port |
| `*_METRICS_URL` | none | Each value is one catalog source |

The compose file sets `MONGO_URI=mongodb://dashboard-db:27017/contractsdb`, but `infra/db.rs` always opens `crowdvision`. The `contractsdb` in the URI is ignored.

---

## What it stores

| Where | Shape | Lifetime |
|---|---|---|
| MongoDB `crowdvision.preferences` | `{_id, building_id, allowed_columns: [String]}`, unique on `building_id` | Until removed by hand. Nothing deletes a building's entry |
| `DashMap` in memory | `building_id → [String]` | Process lifetime, filled from MongoDB at start |

---

## Metrics

| Name | Type | Counts |
|---|---|---|
| `telemetry_events_received_total` | counter | Ticks parsed from `telemetry:raw` |
| `telemetry_events_published_total` | counter | Ticks forwarded to a building channel |
| `telemetry_fanout_latency_ms` | histogram, buckets 5 to 1000 | `ingestedAt` to forward time |

---

## Tests

```bash
just test dashboard               # unit, no MongoDB or Redis needed
just test dashboard-integration   # tests/*.rs against throwaway MongoDB and Redis
```

| Where | Checks |
|---|---|
| `src/tunnel.rs` | `resolve_channel`: own building's channel; any metric forwarded; unknown building dropped; never another building's channel; a non-tick does not parse |
| `src/api/data.rs`, `init.rs` | Save stores, overwrites, accepts an empty list; init gives exactly `roomName`, `roomMaxOccupancy`; a second init keeps the columns. Run against an unconnected collection: the write is fire and forget, so no MongoDB is needed |
| `src/api/dashboard.rs` | `push_unique_metric` cases (6 metrics with 2 duplicates give 4); both catalog forms fill `source`; an unparseable, unreachable or slow source is skipped while the others stay |
| `src/infra/claims.rs` | Valid claims; URL-safe base64; missing, malformed, no `sub`: `401` |
| `src/infra/discovery.rs` | Only `*_METRICS_URL` keys are read |
| `tests/tunnel.rs` | Real Redis: a tick republished byte for byte; a building with no columns dropped; a non-tick does not stop the loop |
| `tests/db.rs` | Real MongoDB: upsert then load; upsert replaces; empty collection is empty, not an error |

`moon.yml` pins `test` to `cargo test --lib`, so `just test all` passes with nothing running.

---

## Gaps

- **No access check per building.** Any signed-in person can read or overwrite any building's columns.
- **A saved column can be lost.** `200` comes before the MongoDB write.
- **No delete.** A removed building keeps its entry in MongoDB and in memory, and its ticks keep being forwarded.
- **The tunnel never reconnects** after a Redis restart.
